Subject: [PATCH 0/3] ASoC: qcom: no path around speaker protection

Requires a checked tweeter high-pass ahead of SP RX, limits the WSA mix
path gain, and forbids remixing or gain after SP RX.

 1/3 ASoC: qcom: require a checked tweeter high-pass in front of SP RX
     Author: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
     Not posted.
 2/3 ASoC: qcom: x1e80100: also limit the WSA mix path digital volumes
     Author: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
     Not posted.
 3/3 ASoC: qcom: audioreach: nothing after SP RX may remix or amplify
     Author: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
     Not posted.

From a9b7034298c70337b7184503370423895a245ac5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:14:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] ASoC: qcom: require a checked tweeter high-pass in front of
 SP RX

SP RX's own high-pass is a single ~80 Hz filter on all channels, so a
stream that bypasses a userspace crossover reaches the tweeters full
band. As on Windows, high-pass the tweeters in the DSP with an MSIIR
ahead of SP, and have the kernel check it.

When the machine driver lists tweeters, SP RX only runs behind an MSIIR
whose blob high-passes exactly the tweeter lanes, and nothing may join
the chain downstream of the filter. Blobs that would change the SP
modes, R0/T0 or test modes the kernel owns are refused.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
