From 3b48ab489db674ae46d5b295028413340e6b530c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:02:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: nothing after SP RX may remix or
 amplify

audioreach_sp_rx_chain() accepts any single-link chain between SP RX and
the WSA RX0 codec DMA sink, so a channel mixer, volume or gain module
there can swap woofer and tweeter lanes or add gain after SP and the
tweeter high-pass, undoing both.

When speaker protection is required, allow only the MFC right after SP,
which restores lane order and may not carry a cfg blob, and data logging
modules.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
index 5168d803ca83..4127316b09d1 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
